s:\n- **Who made the request:** `clientip`, `agent`, `machine.os`.\n- **What was requested:** `url`, `request`, `extension`, `referer`.\n- **The result:** `response`, which is the HTTP status code stored as text with a keyword copy, and `bytes`.\n- **Where from and to:** `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`.\n- **Other:** `tags`, `memory` and `hour_of_day`.\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-62fc3433 Web logs overview\"** has 7 panels:\n- Total requests\n- Unique visitors (distinct client IPs)\n- Total bytes served\n- Requests over time, split by response code\n- Share of each response code (pie chart)\n- Top 10 URLs, with request count and bytes\n- Top 10 source countries\n\nLink: http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-62fc3433-web-logs-overview-1c7030342ad6\n\n**3. Alert rule \"EFF-62fc3433 5xx spike\"** (id `43c0fa86-4fa2-463c-bd9c-6ac7659ced85`):\n- It runs every minute against `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n- It counts requests whose `response.keyword` is between \"500\" and \"599\" over the last 5 minutes, and fires when that count is above 10.\n- Kibana confirms it is saved and enabled. Its first run was still pending when I checked.\n- It has no notification actions, so it will create alerts but not send anything. You'd need to add a connector, such as Slack or email, for that.\n\nThe 500–599 range is a text comparison, not a numeric one. It works because status codes are always three digits.","ttft_ms":1986,"type":"result","duration_ms":38697,"uuid":"184eebdd-b93c-4d0f-8085-0ef1e4414841","ttft_stream_ms":1700,"time_to_request_ms":86,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":22,"system_prompt":7,"resume_other":1,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":9,"input_hooks":4,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":2,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":5,"request_build":11},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_